title: 'P8-D96: the tool-permission channel is stream-json can_use_tool (host + stdio), the card is the gate'
summary: 'Chosen over a kernel PermissionRequest hook in policy.json, which would cost a process per prompt and add a second channel. Every can_use_tool request becomes a permission (allow|deny) or plan card and gets exactly one kernel answer; updatedInput is the kernel-held input; never updatedPermissions, never Claude permission_suggestions. Fail closed everywhere (no broker, raise failure, expiry, cancel, duplicate id, exit, pending cap 64). A permit never means allow (P8-D92). AskUserQuestion is denied with "ask in your reply" for this slice. No clientApiId move. Residual: allow rules in any loaded layer and PreToolUse allow hooks bypass the card (p01b h/i); fix candidate: permissions.ask for mutating tools in policy.json.'
